{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1199,
    "dDurationMs": 3761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mountains tend to be narrower at the top than\nthey are at the bottom – otherwise they’ll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4960,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eventually fall down – but that doesn’t\nmean that mountains are always SMALLER at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8350,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the top. Because, what matters to most land\ncreatures is the amount of land; that is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12820,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the surface area, not the volume –  unless\nyou’re a mining company that plans to pulverize"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16410,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the entire mountain into smithereens. Then\nvolume matters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19110,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to the rest of us, we care about surface\narea – and surprisingly, the area of land"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23910,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a mountain doesn’t necessarily get smaller\nas you go higher up the mountain – especially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28500,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when that mountain is part of a mountain range,\nas mountains tend to be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32150,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Simple, lone mountains with shapes like cones\nor spikes or inverted parabolas do indeed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36750,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have less surface area the higher up you go,\nthough a parabolic mountain has a lot more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "area high up than a spikey mountain. And broader,\nflatter, mountains can actually have MORE"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45400,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "area the higher you go up, at least until\nyou get to the very top. These mountains do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49650,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get skinnier as they go up, but they get flatter\nso much faster than they get skinnier that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54130,
    "dDurationMs": 4269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the perspective of available surface\narea they’re bigger on top than at the bottom!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58399,
    "dDurationMs": 4231,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when you put mountains together into RANGES,\nit’s even more complicated. Some ranges"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62630,
    "dDurationMs": 5650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have LESS land area the higher you go up,\nsome have MORE area, some have more and then"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68280,
    "dDurationMs": 4829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less, and some actually have more area at\nboth the bottom and top and less area in the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73109,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "middle!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74109,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, if you do a survey of mountain ranges\nthe world over, you’ll find that only around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77409,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a third of them have a constantly decreasing\namount of land the higher you go, and the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81359,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rest exhibit one of the other weird “top-heavy”\noptions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84539,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, despite appearances and as\nodd as it sounds, MOST mountain ranges are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89459,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bigger near their tops. Which has interesting\nimplications for any land-dwelling creatures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94109,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that might want to move their homes and businesses\nup or down mountains, if, I don’t know,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97539,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the climate changes or something."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100479,
    "dDurationMs": 5301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And one more weird fact: a perfectly hemispherical\nmountain, while impossible in reality, has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105780,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just the right shape to get skinnier at the\nsame rate that it gets flatter, so it has,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110009,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amazingly, the exact same amount of area at\nevery elevation. The same math also means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114929,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that if you evenly slice an orange, each piece\nwill have roughly the same amount of skin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119079,
    "dDurationMs": 15711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– but different amounts "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134790,
    "dDurationMs": 18569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of fruit."
    } ]
  } ]
}
